From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:45:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 133/342] meson_vdec: H.264 as tested: aligned buffers, a
 warm-up, the end, seeks

- Buffers aligned to their size (at most 1 MB), as Linux's are: the H.264
  firmware failed with every workspace aligned to 4 KB only.
- The first H.264 session after boot decoded the first macroblock's luma
  wrongly (all pictures up to the next IDR picture with it): it starts with
  a session of its own that decodes a 16x16 picture, after which the
  decoder is right until the next boot.
- Frames given back wait in a queue for the firmware's two places: it stops
  taking them at the end of the stream's picture. The end is when the
  firmware read all before that picture and reported nothing for 100 ms.
- The buffers stay from session to session (until the device is closed):
  a seek starts a session, which took 140 ms to find tens of megabytes of
  contiguous memory; and nothing is logged per session (the serial output
  of the trace took 330 ms).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
